// Routing fixtures for jitx-component-modeler: should-trigger / should-not-trigger phrasings.
// Positives paraphrase real user phrasing across both lanes the skill owns — the
// single-named-part lane, and the parameterized-family lane where one class stands
// in for a catalog series ("the class is the data, no parts DB"). Negatives are
// near-misses that share
// component vocabulary but belong to a sibling skill. Line 2 is byte-identical to the
// negative the substrate-modeler's fixtures already route here; the two files must agree.
{"intent": "build me parameterized component families from these two datasheets — no parts DB, the class should be the data so I can ask for any part in the catalog and get the MPN", "expected_skill": "jitx-component-modeler"}
{"intent": "model this part from the datasheet — QFN-48, thermal pad", "expected_skill": "jitx-component-modeler"}
{"intent": "one class per manufacturer family — every case size in the series, tolerance and packaging axes, and the vendor's own part-number encoder", "expected_skill": "jitx-component-modeler"}
{"intent": "add an MLCC family on the same helpers so I can ask for 100 nF X7R 0603 50 V and get an orderable part number", "expected_skill": "jitx-component-modeler"}
{"intent": "which of the two termination bands on this chip resistor outline drawing goes in the land pattern?", "expected_skill": "jitx-component-modeler"}
{"intent": "I need an LM1117 in the 8-pin WSON — here's the TI datasheet", "expected_skill": "jitx-component-modeler"}
{"intent": "generate the RP2040 component, all 56 pins plus the exposed pad", "expected_skill": "jitx-component-modeler"}
{"intent": "make a JITX component for C165948, LCSC has the footprint", "expected_skill": "jitx-component-modeler"}
{"intent": "convert this .kicad_mod into a JITX landpattern for a board-to-board connector the generators can't express", "expected_skill": "jitx-component-modeler"}
